module gunbc.p3a1_self_fork_homonym_disposition

data p3a1_bit_homonym_hold_note: String = "P3a-1 HOLD (parent ruling msg_41dbc4b4): the Bit census row is a measurement artifact, not a production co-resolution defect. The failing diagnostic is fixture-vs-fixture — synthetic.parse_mechanism.nest_d1..nest_d4 each declare 'type Bit = B0 | B1' in four independent modules that never co-resolve in any real compilation; they collide only inside the forced whole-corpus synthetic closure. Under namespace-only resolution their qualified names differ (nest_d1.Bit vs nest_d2.Bit, etc.), so no rename is warranted. Renaming all four to one shared name would leave four MechanismBit declarations and preserve the collision verbatim."

data p3a1_condition_homonym_hold_note: String = "P3a-1 HOLD (parent ruling msg_41dbc4b4): examples.interp_test.Condition and examples.weather.Condition are independent example modules that never import each other. They are ambiguous only inside the forced whole-corpus synthetic closure; qualified names differ under namespace-only end state. No rename."

data p3a1_production_homonym_caveat_note: String = "P3a-1 caveat (parent ruling msg_41dbc4b4): the whole-corpus census cannot prove any production pair is genuinely co-resolved in a real closure — the synthetic root forces everything together. The authoritative ambiguity population comes from the compiler fold over real closures. KeySource, JsonValue, and YamlValue renames in this lane are safe because they are live production carriers with verified overlapping consumers, not because the census count alone established co-resolution."
